            <ArticleTitle>Right atrial aneurysm treated with atrioplasty without using cardiopulmonary bypass in an infant.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>343-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A 7-month-old female child was diagnosed to have a massive right atrial aneurysm, presented with arrhythmias. She was treated by restorative right atrioplasty without using cardiopulmonary bypass. She had good postoperative outcome and a 5-month follow-up remains uneventful. In the absence of major congenital heart defects, aneurysm of right atrium can be treated without using cardiopulmonary bypass.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
